  "sleepHowBody1": "The app counts the longest stretch your phone sits untouched overnight as sleep, between 6 pm and 2 pm the next day, lasting 3 to 16 hours. A stretch that ends before 1 am, like charging in the evening, only counts when nothing that night lasts past 1 am.",
  "@sleepHowBody1": {
    "description": "Sleep explainer paragraph (Android)"
  },
  "sleepHowBody1Ios": "The app takes the longest sleep your iPhone or Apple Watch saved in Health between 6 pm and 2 pm the next day. Sleep under 3 hours or over 16 hours doesn't count. Sleep that ends before 1 am only counts when nothing that night lasts past 1 am.",
  "@sleepHowBody1Ios": {
    "description": "Sleep explainer paragraph (iOS)"
  },
  "sleepHowBody2": "Picking up your phone for under 5 minutes counts as waking up, not as the end of your sleep.",
  "@sleepHowBody2": {
    "description": "Sleep explainer paragraph (Android)"
  },
  "sleepHowBody3": "It's an estimate: watching a movie in bed or leaving your phone elsewhere can skew it. You can fix it within 7 days, and your person will see an “Edited” label.",
  "@sleepHowBody3": {
    "description": "Sleep explainer paragraph"
  },
  "sleepHowBody4": "The app reads no content on your phone, only when the screen turns on or off.",
  "@sleepHowBody4": {
    "description": "Sleep explainer paragraph (Android)"
  },
  "sleepHowBody4Ios": "The app only reads Sleep in Health, nothing else.",
  "@sleepHowBody4Ios": {
    "description": "Sleep explainer paragraph (iOS)"
  },
  "sleepHowIphoneInBed": "Your iPhone can log time in bed by itself: open Health → Browse → Sleep → Sleep Schedule, set a bedtime and turn on tracking time in bed with iPhone. Some iPhones on iOS 18 or later no longer offer this.",
  "@sleepHowIphoneInBed": {
    "description": "Sleep explainer paragraph (iOS): Sleep Schedule / time in bed"
  },
  "sleepHowMotion": "If you let the app see motion, nights with nothing recorded are guessed from when your phone lay still. It is only a guess: a phone left on the desk all morning may be counted as sleep, and you can fix it by hand. Raw motion data stays on your phone; your person only sees sleep and wake times if you turn sharing on.",
  "@sleepHowMotion": {
    "description": "Sleep explainer paragraph: motion fallback (both platforms)"
  },
  "sleepGotIt": "Got it",
